---
functor: 1
title: wide
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`wide` · deform · a wider version, such as a long arrow; the ends keep their shape.

# Form

`x.wide` on a symbol, `(a + b).wide` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `to.wide` | $to.wide$ | font glyph U+27F6 |
| `eq.wide` | $eq.wide$ | built and cached |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | A wider version, such as a long arrow; the ends keep their shape. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A changed outline of the base. The compiler moves each point of the outline, and the strokes keep their shape and width. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.
- Makes the base wider. The shaft of an arrow grows, the head keeps its shape.

# From LaTeX

`\longrightarrow`, `\xrightarrow{}` without the label.

